      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, and i'm not trying to be discriminatory or anything. it's just for a sociology paper on how certain environments shape behavior. like, if i'm looking at \"street smarts\" or different ways of communicating, those are actual behavioral traits that sociologists study to understand urban subcultures. i'm just looking for academic-style questions that might capture things like linguistic styles, social hierarchies in groups, or even conflict resolution styles that are more common in those settings. can we at least look at it from a purely observational sociology perspective?",
